-- ror-in-rand.l4 with the ROR's alternatives the other way round. L4 runs
-- `b` first: it records `x` at 10, and the ROR is fulfilled when `a` is, at
-- 20. Taken one event at a time, the record is made before `c` reads `x` at
-- 30, so `c` sees it, and the whole is FULFILLED. (smucclaw/l4-ide#1069)

DECLARE Party IS ONE OF P, Q, R
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF actA, actB, actZ, actR

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`a` MEANS
    PARTY P
    MUST actA
    WITHIN 100

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`b` MEANS
    PARTY Q
    MAY actB
    WITHIN 100
    HENCE COMMIT `x` IS TRUE
          HENCE `z`
    LEST FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`z` MEANS
    PARTY Q
    MUST actZ
    WITHIN 100

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`c` MEANS
    PARTY R
    MUST actR PROVIDED (RECALL OFFICIAL's `x`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
    WITHIN 40
    HENCE COMMIT `c saw x` IS TRUE HENCE FULFILLED

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party Act
`whole` MEANS (`b` ROR `a`) RAND `c`

#TRACE `whole` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Q DOES actB AT 10
    PARTY P DOES actA AT 20
    PARTY R DOES actR AT 30
    PARTY P DOES actA AT 50
